cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "bitflipsim: single-event-upset injection, per-bit criticality and mitigation accounting for small scikit-learn / ONNX inference models"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Bit-level single-event-upset injection into the parameters and activations of
  a small scikit-learn or ONNX inference model, with the IEEE 754 and
  two's-complement storage layouts discovered at runtime rather than asserted;
  a flux times cross-section times bit-count rate model with Poisson counts and
  their sampling errors; exhaustive per-bit criticality by storage position for
  float32 and int8; a learned criticality predictor with an ensemble
  uncertainty output, benchmarked against a magnitude baseline and an
  exponent-bit heuristic on degradation avoided per protected byte; and
  mitigation evaluation covering parameter range clamping with a derived and
  exhaustively verified deviation bound, selective triplication with two
  majority voters enumerated over all single and double upsets, and periodic
  reload, each with its memory and latency cost. Validation level 2,
  research grade. This software models upsets; it does not qualify parts. Not
  flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - single-event-upset
  - radiation-effects
  - fault-injection
  - bit-flip
  - ieee-754
  - triple-modular-redundancy
  - onnx
  - onboard-inference
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    authors:
      - family-names: Mahmoud
        given-names: A.
      - family-names: Aggarwal
        given-names: N.
      - family-names: Nobbe
        given-names: A.
      - family-names: "Sanchez Vicarte"
        given-names: "J. R."
      - family-names: Adve
        given-names: "S. V."
      - family-names: Fletcher
        given-names: "C. W."
      - family-names: Frosio
        given-names: I.
      - family-names: Hari
        given-names: "S. K. S."
    title: "PyTorchFI: A Runtime Perturbation Tool for DNNs"
    collection-title: "2020 50th Annual IEEE/IFIP International Conference on Dependable Systems and Networks Workshops (DSN-W)"
    start: 25
    end: 31
    year: 2020
    notes: >-
      Named in this repository's alternatives table as the closest prior art.
      The bibliographic details above are those given in the citation block of
      the pytorchfi project description on PyPI, read on 2026-10-05.
  - type: standard
    title: "IEEE Standard for Floating-Point Arithmetic"
    number: "IEEE 754-2019"
    institution:
      name: "IEEE"
    year: 2019
    notes: >-
      The binary16, binary32 and binary64 interchange formats. This repository
      does not quote the standard; it derives every layout field from numpy at
      runtime and re-derives it from probe encodings, so the layout is checked
      rather than asserted (validation/validate_ieee754_layout.py).
